Based on the XAI edge extractions for Dataset 1, the architecture successfully identified 
subtle behavioral coping mechanisms and latent emotional states rather than just memorizing e
xplicitly sad vocabulary. Looking at the global connections, it captured feelings of social 
exhaustion by linking the concept of "exist" to "hangout" and strongly weighted a tweet about 
isolating to listen to grunge/metal music the "whole" day. However, the true power 
of your Tri-Model-Fusion is demonstrated in the semantic document-to-document bridges: 
it mathematically clustered tweets about passive, isolated observation 
(watching birds and dogs at the park) into the exact same psychological space, while correctly grouping socially active, positive tweets (friends bursting into laughter) into their own distinct cluster. Furthermore, the strong self-loop on the tweet expressing feeling "unappreciated" and "crappy" proves that your underlying GoEmotions and MentalRoBERTa embeddings are so robust at capturing raw emotional distress that the network can definitively diagnose severe depressive affect based purely on the initial feature vector, without even needing to rely on neighborhood context. 



